⌇⡧⢵⣘⠨


Latin/abbrev ※⡧⢈⢟⠢
  SEE https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Latin_abbreviations
  ALSO:(syntax): .(by|same|like|and).



main()
  af/a4 = after  IDEA:(syntax combi): a4yyday="after the day before yesterday"
  bc = because (∵ <<)
  bf/b4 = before
  bnf = back'n'forth
  bw = between
  cpl = compile[ation]
  efi-y = efficiently
  efe-y = effectively
  # evb = everybody
  # evd/evy = everyday
  # ev1 = everyone
~ evels = "everything else"
~ evg (evr/evt/evg/evrt/evtg/evth/evng) = "everything"
  # evrw/evr~ = everywhere
  hwr/hwer = however
  iav = interactive[ly]
  iff = if and only if
  imm = immediate[ly]
  inad = in addition to  # OLD=inat
  inof = instead of
  iow = in other words
  ivt = invariant
  lgtm = «looks good to me» OR =[l]e[g]i[t]i[m]ate
  mo = modus operandi # (method/practices of operating)
  no. = number
  orse = otherwise
  rec/recm = rec[ommendation]
  recd = rec[or]d
  rev = review        # (<most usable eng-word with this pfx)
  sa = sensu amplo    # (=in relaxed/generous/ample sense)
  sl = sensu lato     # (=in wide/broad sense)
  ss = sensu stricto  # (=strictly speaking)
~ smwr = somewhere
  tba = to be available/accessible
  tbat/tbato = to be able to
  tf/t4 = therefore (∴ >>)
  tiac = take into account
  vs = versus (agst[against])
  wrt = with regard to


/rec/
  + rec[ommendation] (~recm)
  + recab = recalib[rate]
  + recalc[ulate]
  + recap = recap | recapitulate | ~recapture
  + recat[alog][ing]
  + recd = rec[or]d
  + recfg = reconfigur[ation]
  + recomb[ine]
  + recon = reconnaissance (ALSO: recce|recco|reccy)
  + recr[eat][ional]
  + rect[angle]
  + rectif[iable]
  + recur[rent|sive]
  + recv = receive*
  ? recn = recent
  ? recol = recol[lect][ion] | reconcile[ment] | recall
  ? reconn[ect]*
  ? recop = reconceptualiz[ation]
  ? recoz = recognizable
  ? recp = recipe | receipt* | recipient | reception*
  ? repn = reception
  ? ress = recess* | recede | recis[s]ion | recusabl[eant]
  . recip. = reciproc[al|ation]
  . recirc[ulate]
  . recls = reclassification
  . recnt = recount* (~recot)
  . recup[erat][ion]
  . recyc[lable]
  ~ recdr = reconsider[ation]
  ~ recdv = recidiv[ate]
  ~ recf = recification | reconfirmation
  ~ recg = recharge
  ~ rechk = recheck
  ~ recl = recalled | reclaim*
  ~ recog = recognition
  ~ recos = reconstruction
  ~ recov[erable]
  ~ recylz = recrystallization
  ~ rmc = recommence[ment] | =resume/возобновление/возрождение
